import { Cossack, State, Server, Optimistic, optimistic, RpcError, isUncertainRpcError } from '@cossackframework/core';
class Counter extends Cossack {
 @State() count=0;
 @Server() async add(amount:number):Promise<number>{this.count+=amount;return this.count;}
 @Optimistic('add') preview(amount:number){optimistic<Counter>(this).increment('count',amount);}
}
if(!isUncertainRpcError(new RpcError('COSSACK_RPC_TIMEOUT','Deadline expired')))throw new Error('Timeout must remain uncertain');
if(isUncertainRpcError(new RpcError('COSSACK_VALIDATION_FAILED','Validation failed',{status:400})))throw new Error('Validation rejection is known');
export type CounterResult=Awaited<ReturnType<Counter['add']>>;

guides.markdown:
rpc$ accepts a browser server-method proxy call (or its factory) as RpcCall: await it for the terminal result and use for await for intermediate yields. Awaiting and iterating share one invocation. Duplicate consumers do not create independent executions; cleanup, timeout and cancellation belong to that shared call. Use the declared Server timeout policy and pass cancellation to I/O; ignored remote work may still finish. Read stable RpcError codes rather than parsing exception text. Native Response actions use the explicit response contract and byte bounds.

@Page transport selects HTTP, SSE or Durable Object/WebSocket integration. HTTP is stateless; SSE carries server-to-client updates with HTTP actions. Node realtime state is process-local; it is not Cloudflare durable state. CossackDurableObject is an infrastructure integration point requiring real bindings; @Page scope, computed and rechecked on the server, selects the one realtime instance a page connects to. Never infer durability from a transport name. Socket peers and delivered operations must be authorized against trusted server context, including after connection.

The example defines typed consumption for a transformed browser proxy and executes rejection of an ordinary local generator plus capability reporting. rpc$ is not a general generator wrapper. It does not open a socket, prove a server dispatch, or simulate native Durable Object persistence.

