import { storeRules,validateValue,type ValidationRule } from '@cossackframework/core';
interface Address {zip:string;}
const rules=storeRules<Address>({zip:{required:true,minLength:3}});
if(!rules)throw new Error('Typed rule tree was not built');
const quantityRule:ValidationRule={required:true,coerce:'number',min:1};
const empty=validateValue('',quantityRule);
if(empty.valid)throw new Error('Required empty quantity was accepted');
const parsed=validateValue('2',quantityRule);
if(!parsed.valid||parsed.value!==2)throw new Error('Number coercion failed');

guides.markdown:
@Server({input,authorize}) runs the declared authorizer on parsed input before invoking an inbound action. Return true or false, or throw a deliberate authorization denial. Read trusted authenticated context and load record ownership server-side; never accept a submitted user ID, client State or socket attachment as proof of access. Authorizers receive AbortSignal and must pass it to cancellable I/O. A disconnected or cancelled caller does not prove a write was rolled back.

@Shared marks intentional server/client logic, not an inbound remote endpoint. createTypedDecorators supports authored channel contracts for State and Server. Client handlers and optimistic previews cannot enforce security. Realtime peers must be rechecked for inbound actions and delivered operations; revocation must stop later access even when a socket remains open. Socket request snapshots are bounded context evidence, not retained Request objects or client authority.

getAuthorizationFailure yields fixed unauthenticated/forbidden diagnostics, omitting authored exception messages and values. Unexpected exceptions stay private; ClientVisibleError is only for deliberately public wording and ActionValidationError for intended field errors. The example proves fixed denial redaction and accessor avoidance; real dispatch-policy execution belongs to generated native transport acceptance.

examples.source:
import { getAuthorizationFailure,ClientVisibleError,ActionValidationError,isActionValidationError } from '@cossackframework/core';
let reads=0;
const denied={authorizationCode:'COSSACK_AUTH_FORBIDDEN',message:'PRIVATE_PROVIDER_VALUE'};
const denial=getAuthorizationFailure(denied);
if(denial?.status!==403||denial.message!=='Forbidden'||JSON.stringify(denial).includes('PRIVATE_PROVIDER_VALUE'))throw new Error('Authorization denial leaked');
const hostile={};Object.defineProperty(hostile,'authorizationCode',{get(){reads++;throw new Error('PRIVATE_GETTER');}});
if(getAuthorizationFailure(hostile)!==undefined||reads!==0)throw new Error('Denial getter was invoked');
const expected=new ActionValidationError({email:'Use a valid email'});
if(!(expected instanceof ClientVisibleError)||!isActionValidationError(expected))throw new Error('Expected field error lost its public contract');
